    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0576" n="504" xml:id="pg504"/>

                <head>No. 310.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wallace to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 21, 1882</date>.
                        (Received April 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 74.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. B. O. Duncan, while visiting the city
                    last week, informed me that the customs officers at Smyrna were continuing to
                    collect a duty upon alcohol in excess of the rate specifically agreed upon under
                    the treaty. Inclosed please find a copy of a note which I will to-day send to
                    the Porte upon the subject.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LEW. WALLACE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d374-a1.xml" xpointer="d374-a1"/>
            </div>
